      "onUnknown": "BODY_LANGUAGE_SOURCE_VARIANT_UNKNOWN",
      "selectionLaw": "TypeScript has no per-crate dialect map; its per-body axis is the SOURCE VARIANT its own file suffix denotes, which decides how the body is scanned and parsed. Longest matching suffix wins, so .d.ts is never read as .ts. An unlisted suffix REFUSES rather than being folded into a neighbouring variant, so a normal variant is never silently mis-assigned and a new one must be registered deliberately. Distinct suffixes stay distinct even where a parser would treat two alike: this can fail to equate two bodies that are in fact equivalent, and can never equate two the language reads differently. Collapsing variants is a claim about a parser and belongs to the level specification. Only the variant token enters the record; the path does not."
     },
