      "cjs": "javascript"
     },
     "bodyLanguageLaw": "The body languageId is DERIVED from the selected source variant, not from the provider universe. The universe language is the engine that reads the body; a .js body read by the TypeScript engine is a javascript body and must carry that identifier, exactly as native section 6.3 requires. The frame languageId and the record languageId are both taken from this one selector over the same anchor, so they cannot disagree. No JavaScript body is rewritten as TypeScript, and the cross-tsjs candidate projection of section 6.4 is untouched."
    }
